    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d195">

                <pb facs="0479" n="431" xml:id="pg431"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Thornton</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-07-23"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 23, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to transmit herewith, for
                    your information and that of the government which you represent, a copy of an
                        instruction<anchor n="*" xml:id="d195-f1"/> which, on the 14th instant, was
                    addressed by this department to the United States minister at Yeddo.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, with the highest consideration, your obedient
                    servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward Thornton,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c.</hi>,
                            <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d195-f1" n="*" xml:id="d195-f1-content">
                <p>For this inclosure see correspondence with. United States minister to Japan.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
